[?2004l3:Mixed meeting notes, mail excerpts, policy exceptions, and ledger rows.
5:## Reconciliation and Exception Policy (FY24 Audit Handbook)
7:effective_date on output is YYYY-MM-DD. Start from the ledger date field.
8:When a correction notice sets field date or status, use the notice effective
9:date as effective_date only if that correction modified status or date;
10:otherwise keep ledger date.
12:Use only the section whose heading is exactly ## Transaction Ledger.
13:Ignore other ledger-like sections and any ledger block with provisional: true.
15:If the same transaction id appears in more than one ledger block, the last
19:Ledger provides base status (lowercase on output). Email excerpts may change
22:change only if sent is greater than or equal to the ledger date. When no sent:
24:Correction notices apply last; when multiple notices target the same
28:notice applies (after ledger, amendments, and emails).
30:Owner precedence: ledger owner is the default. Meeting note amendments under
33:greater than or equal to the ledger date. Correction notices for field owner
36:amount_usd is numeric from ledger, two decimal places in CSV, JSON number.
38:exception_reason is null unless an exception applies: set over_limit when
39:amount_usd strictly exceeds 10000; set compliance_hold when final status is
42:amount_usd > 10000, and a Policy Exception block exists for that txn with
44:amount_usd > 5000, and a winning correction notice changed status for that txn.
50:(JSON number, two decimal places), exception_reason (null or semicolon-joined
52:transaction_id,owner,status,effective_date,amount_usd,exception_reason with the
53:same rows and order; leave exception_reason blank when null. exceptions.json is
54:{"items":[...]} (not {"exceptions":...}) with only rows where exception_reason
55:is set. reconciliation_report.jsonl is one JSON object per winning correction
61:archive mentions section titles in prose and includes decoy ledger headings.
